# structgen arguments for sdk/ts/gen/msg_layout.bots.ts: the iMessage envelope's
# header (c/src/msg_wire.h MsgHeader), which the FMSG bridge reads after a decode
# and fills in before a seal. A snapshot reader and a writer - plain objects
# copied out of and back into the module, no accessor over the struct - and the
# codec's own constants and refusal codes, so no bridge restates a cap or a
# number. Read by tools/structgen/gen.sh with --cwd c/ and the bots build's
# flags. The root is in game_layout.args too, so the layout hash bots.wasm is
# checked against at load covers these readers.
#
# The browser reaches this module (the /m/ route decodes an envelope), which is
# why it is not in game_layout.bots.ts - that one holds accessors over the
# unmasked Game and e2e/security_client_boundary keeps it out of the bundle.
--header msg_wire.h --root MsgHeader --snapshot MsgHeader --writer MsgHeader --snapshot-only
--fields MsgEnvelope=format,flags,phase,game_id,turn,last_actor_seat,n_players,variant,round,parent8,seed,sent_at,n_new,opening,carry_key,carry_fool,n_joins,joins
--count MsgEnvelope.joins=n_joins --count MsgJoin.name=name_len
#
# And the replay code's extras (replay_extras.h ReplayExtras) - the nicknames and
# per-move timing behind the dash in a share link - which the same bridge crosses
# with in both directions. Not the codec's own packed blob: that is a C format,
# packed and unpacked beside it (replay_extras_pack).
--header replay_extras.h --root ReplayExtras --snapshot ReplayExtras --writer ReplayExtras
--count ReplayExtras.names=n_names --count ReplayExtras.gaps=n_gaps --count ReplayExtrasName.text=len
--const MSG_ --const REPLAY_EXTRAS_ --const REPLAY_LINK_STYLE_
